From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Xun2202 <98207886+Xun2202@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 16:49:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] update: let manual checks work with auto-check off and fix
 the new-version popup
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- The settings page's "check for updates" button went through the same
  autoCheckUpdate gate as the automatic check, so turning automatic checks
  off also disabled manual ones (the button flashed "checking" and fell
  straight back to "check for updates"). Only automatic checks honour the
  setting now, and a manual check that finds nothing says "up to date".
- The release notes in the new-version card were a plain Column inside a
  dialog that cannot scroll, so long notes pushed the buttons off screen.
  The notes now scroll inside a bounded area.
- Fork release notes list every patch plus install instructions; only the
  "本次变更" section is a changelog. Parse that section and fall back to
  the whole body for releases that predate it.
- The "in-app download" switch stays enabled when automatic checks are off,
  since manual downloads use it too; the popup's download button reads
  "Update now" instead of "Auto-update"; "view changelog" opens the fork's
  release page for -harmony versions.
- Android deletes the installer of the running version at startup, as
  desktop already did; the APK no longer lingers in cache/updates/download.
